*vertical translations** to the graph of ![](images/e3/e31f27c483c52d7933201e37d1f6020c20d7903402be16f28ffd407c7f3db93a.svg).\n\n- The graph of ![](images/91/91c9b5c48d46f81336e889febab90a9027a96accef8626bd0743ca81042f25b8.svg) is a **vertical translation** of the absolute value graph ![](images/0c/0cb4d1ae0c2e2451edd095b9dbcca94222e8ef0514db46745a2acce4b617d78e.svg) It moves the graph ![](images/34/349015631ec44ef653936c85586d2c5ef56ba64392b3f92b4b92cbef3e731bc5.svg) units up.\n\n![](images/cd/cd8b826034f7c3668cacb490e0fab60daaf7c5cae63975bfa5cae9d468c7dec6.png)\n\n- The graph of ![](images/30/3016548be8be38ace3450d51a10371543820a3357b1adbf809d69c23c70f14bb.svg) is a **horizontal translation** of the absolute value graph ![](images/0c/0cb4d1ae0c2e2451edd095b9dbcca94222e8ef0514db46745a2acce4b617d78e.svg) It moves the graph ![](images/34/349015631ec44ef653936c85586d2c5ef56ba64392b3f92b4b92cbef3e731bc5.svg) units to the *right*.\n\n![](images/65/65912d2831dd525964b78a20f2a707d7d828daa2a5e2ebd0793c6b337a42e360.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- When drawing horizontal and vertical translations, it is easiest to transform the graph's vertex first. Then, the two branches can be drawn coming out of the vertex.\n\n- When we translate the graph ![](images/87/87f4b5227cb69bd468d75d826fe448c91ae677181f9142fcbe9bc757d0acea77.svg) the resulting curve is called the **image** of ![](images/e3/e31f27c483c52d7933201e37d1f6020c20d7903402be16f28ffd407c7f3db93a.svg) under the translation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1065 9295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1b8dce6a-8742-581b-80f6-e39c9943b395" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1064 "Horizontal and vertical translations can be combined. It does not matter which we do first.\n\nIn general, the graph of $y=|x-h|+k$ is a translation of the graph $y=|x|$ by\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n\n- $k$ units up." #